  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira's contrast CT is ordered for his Monday 10/26 9:00 slot. I set up the prep RBC-RAD-07 requires, held his metformin and sent him instructions.\n\n**What I did**\n- **CT order:** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001), placed for the booked slot and linked to the appointment (appt-00001).\n- **Contrast allergy:** His allergy list shows iohexol with \"anaphylaxis.\" That label was added in 2021 from his own account, and no records were checked. The 2019 St. Brigid radiology report from the day of the scan describes hives and mild eyelid swelling, with no breathing or airway symptoms, and the radiologist rated it moderate. The policy says to grade by that day-of record, so his premedication follows the rule for a prior mild or moderate reaction. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies don't count as contrast risks.\n- **Premedication:**\n  - Prednisone 50 mg by mouth at 8:00 PM Sunday 10/25, then 2:00 AM and 8:00 AM Monday 10/26 (mr-t0003).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth at 8:00 AM Monday (mr-t0004).\n- **Kidney function:** He needs a recent creatinine because he's 64 and has diabetes. The ED creatinines from 10/16–17 (1.94, then 1.46) were drawn during acute kidney injury, so they don't count, and the 9/24 value (1.02) is from before the injury. I ordered a new creatinine to be drawn between now and 8:30 AM Monday (sr-t0002). Per policy the scan goes ahead as booked, and the radiologist reviews the result that day.\n- **Metformin:** The 10/17 ED summary shows acute kidney injury that hadn't returned to baseline at discharge. I put metformin on hold (mr-00189) from now until at least 48 hours after the scan. I ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006). I also created a task for you, due 10/30, to review it and restart metformin only if kidney function is normal (task-t0007). That draw also covers the one-week kidney recheck the ED asked for.\n- **Patient message:** I sent him an urgent portal message (comm-t0008). It covers:\n  - the blood draw before the scan\n  - the exact times for each dose\n  - no driving after the diphenhydramine, so he needs a driver\n  - stopping metformin now and not restarting until we tell him\n  - drinking fluids, when to call, and when to call 911\n- **Chart note:** I signed a note recording all of this (doc-t0009).\n\n**Left for you:** I didn't edit the iohexol allergy entry, which still says anaphylaxis with high criticality. You or the radiologist may want to update it to match the 2019 report.",
